    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1956992270483198243",
      "url": "https://x.com/LeakedNewsKE/status/1956992270483198243",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/LeakedNewsKE/status/1956992270483198243",
      "text": "Nairobi set for traffic changes as Harambee Stars face Zambia in CHAN 2024 clash\n\nThe National Police Service has issued a traffic advisory ahead of Sunday’s CHAN 2024 clash between Kenya’s Harambee Stars and Zambia’s Chipolopolo, warning motorists of temporary road closures and diversions across Nairobi. \n\nIn a statement posted on X on Saturday, August 16, 2025, police detailed the affected routes and provided alternative paths to help ease traffic during the much-anticipated match. \n\nAccording to the advisory, Aerodrome Road from Madaraka Roundabout to Bunyala Roundabout will be closed, along with one lane of Lang’ata Road from Madaraka Roundabout to Lusaka Roundabout, and one lane of Mombasa Road from Lusaka Roundabout to Bunyala Roundabout. Motorists coming from Mombasa Road heading to the city center are advised to use Likoni Road through Enterprise Road or take the Southern Bypass via Ole Sereni. \n\nThose traveling from Lang’ata Road should use Raila Odinga Road or Muhoho Road via Mbagathi Roundabout. \n\nThe statement also pointed out disruptions along Thika Superhighway and directed motorists to use Kiambu Road at Exit 4, the Northern Bypass, or Ruaka–Baba Ndogo–Lucky Summer–Nairobi River–Mwiki routes depending on their destination. \n\nVehicles heading to Kasarani Stadium without access passes are required to use the Service Lane at Exit 7 or 8. \n\nPolice assured the public that additional officers have been deployed and emphasized that stern action will be taken against anyone violating traffic rules. \n\nThey urged drivers to cooperate with officers on duty to ensure safety and smooth traffic flow. \n\nThe advisory comes as Harambee Stars, already through to the quarter-finals, look to secure the top spot in Group A. \n\nFans have been encouraged to plan their travel early and follow the alternative routes provided to avoid congestion and arrive safely for the high-profile encounter.",
